# AutoRelease Guard — Workspace Rules
# These rules are enforced by all agents and modes in this workspace.

## Commit Format
- All commits MUST follow Conventional Commits spec: https://www.conventionalcommits.org
- Allowed types: feat, fix, chore, ci, docs, refactor, test, perf, build
- Breaking changes require BREAKING CHANGE footer or ! suffix (e.g. feat!:)
- Scope is required for services: feat(api-gateway): ..., fix(worker-service): ...

## Security Output
- All vulnerability findings MUST be emitted as SARIF 2.1.0 JSON
- SARIF output location: reports/security.sarif.json
- Every finding must include: ruleId, level (error/warning/note), message, location (file + line)
- Critical and High findings MUST block the release (no sign-off until resolved or risk-accepted)

## Infrastructure Rules
- No hardcoded secrets, tokens, or credentials in any file (Dockerfile, YAML, .env committed)
- No `privileged: true` in any Kubernetes pod spec
- All containers must have CPU and memory resource limits defined
- All images must be pinned to a digest or specific version tag (no :latest)
- All K8s workloads must have readinessProbe and livenessProbe defined
- Helm charts must use templated image tags, never hardcoded

## Rollback Requirements
- Every release MUST produce ROLLBACK_RUNBOOK.md in artifacts/
- Rollback runbook must include: pre-rollback checklist, rollback commands, smoke test, escalation path
- Rollback commands must be tested in dry-run mode before being written to the runbook

## Release Artifacts
- RELEASE_NOTES.md must follow Keep a Changelog format
- DEPLOY_CHECKLIST.md must be signed off (all items checked) before deploy window opens
- release-readiness.json must aggregate findings from all subagents with a final go/no-go verdict

## Agent Behavior
- Subagents must write their output reports before signaling completion
- The orchestrator (release-planner) must not sign off if any subagent reports CRITICAL findings
- All file paths are relative to the workspace root
- Agents must not modify source files during validation runs — read-only analysis only
- Test synthesizer is the ONLY agent permitted to create new source files (test files only)
